A||N||5||trixterd||The lights go up... don't come down??||||9||
Z||000000||trixterd||04-30-2001||04:12 PM||||We just recently purchased an 86 Fiero.  After a little tinkering we got both lights to smoothly come up when the lights are on... only problem is they don't go back down.  You end up having to lift the hood and manually wind them down.  Any quick tips on how the sensors work for this?||||reg||9
Z||000001||AL||04-30-2001||07:02 PM||||your switch can be the problem,sometimes they go out,if that isn't it, check your relays or change the relays,there is 4 of them, change them out.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||04-30-2001||07:19 PM||||Actually, there are three relays: one mounted on each headlight motor, and the "isolation" relay, located on the driver's side fender.  Incidentally, the switch Al refers to is the headlight switch on the dash, I believe.<P>The white wire on the headlight switch connector should get "+12v," with the switch turned off.  It gets juice from the taillight fuse - so, especially if your taillights aren't working, you need to check to see if the taillight fuse is blown.<P>As Dave Barry likes to say, "I am not making this up."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  For more info on headlight motors, see Michigan Fiero Club webpage.    <BR>  ||||reg||3
Z||000003||Thor||05-02-2001||11:05 PM||||Explain[tinkering]...If the lights go up at the same time but not going down,try this test.  Push the light switch on to raise the headlights. Now push the light switch off[the headlights turn off but don't lower]. Now check the headlight fuse to see if it's blown.If it is you have a short. Replace the fuse and the headlights should go down but you'll still have to find the short. Mine was in the license plate bulb wiring.  If the fuse is not blown then replace the isolation switch relay located on the drivers side fender wall. It's a small black box with wiring coming out of the bottom. Costs about 30 bucks. Remember. You have to locate and repair the short first or you'll just keep blowing the relay.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||05-03-2001||01:13 AM||||With mine, it was the taillight fuse.  As soon as I put a new one in, they went down.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||05-03-2001||07:05 PM||||I test drove an 86 gt like this. It was strange with this one though. If I turned off the headlights they wouldnt go down until I first turned on the parking lights.||||reg||1
